  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "What a Window Function Is",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Definition",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Computes a value across rows related to the current row",
            "Does NOT collapse those rows into one",
            "Aggregate: N rows in, 1 row out",
            "Window: N rows in, N rows out + a new column"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT name, salary,",
            "  AVG(salary) OVER () AS company_avg",
            "FROM employees;  -- 8 rows in, 8 out"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What 'Window' Means",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The window = rows visible to the function right now",
            "Every row gets its own window",
            "Row 3's window may differ from row 4's window"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Families"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Family",
            "Members",
            "Answers"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Aggregate",
              "SUM AVG COUNT MIN MAX",
              "how much"
            ],
            [
              "Ranking",
              "ROW_NUMBER RANK DENSE_RANK",
              "which place"
            ],
            [
              "Ranking+",
              "NTILE PERCENT_RANK CUME_DIST",
              "which slice"
            ],
            [
              "Offset/value",
              "LAG LEAD FIRST_VALUE",
              "neighbour value"
            ],
            [
              "Offset/value",
              "LAST_VALUE NTH_VALUE",
              "edge value"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where It Runs"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Standardised in SQL:2003 — not a vendor extension",
            "PostgreSQL, Oracle, SQL Server 2005+, SQLite 3.25+",
            "MySQL 8.0+, MariaDB 10.2+ (older MySQL: none)",
            "BigQuery, Snowflake, DuckDB all support them"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Canonical Use Cases",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Running totals and moving averages",
            "Rank within group, top-N per group",
            "Period-over-period deltas",
            "Gap detection, deduplication"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Mental model",
          "text": "Query builds a result set first; windows then annotate that set. A post-processing layer, never a filter."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Two names, one thing",
          "items": [
            "'Window function' — standard / PostgreSQL term",
            "'Analytic function' — Oracle and BigQuery term",
            "Same feature, same syntax"
          ],
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Full Grammar",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "func(args) OVER (",
            "  PARTITION BY expr, ...",
            "  ORDER BY expr [ASC|DESC] [NULLS LAST]",
            "  frame_clause )   -- all three optional"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "What a Window Function Is (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "OVER Is the Switch",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A function is a window function only because OVER is attached",
            "SUM(x) and SUM(x) OVER () are different constructs",
            "OVER () with empty parens = one window, every row",
            "Omit OVER and you are back to a plain aggregate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Each Part Does"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Clause",
            "Job"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "PARTITION BY",
              "split into independent groups"
            ],
            [
              "ORDER BY",
              "sequence rows in a partition"
            ],
            [
              "frame_clause",
              "narrow to a moving subset"
            ],
            [
              "(none)",
              "whole result set, one window"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "One Clause, Decomposed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SUM(amount) OVER (",
            "  PARTITION BY customer_id",
            "  ORDER BY order_date",
            "  ROWS UNBOUNDED PRECEDING)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Sum of amount — per customer — in date order",
            "From partition start up to the current row",
            "Drop the frame and the meaning changes silently"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What May Go Inside",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Columns, arithmetic, CASE, function calls: all fine",
            "Other window functions: illegal, no nesting",
            "Composite keys: PARTITION BY region, product_line",
            "Restart happens on each distinct key combination"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Layout",
          "items": [
            "Whitespace inside OVER is free",
            "Break long OVER across lines",
            "One clause per line reads best"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Restart rule",
          "text": "PARTITION BY restarts the function; ORDER BY sequences it; the frame sizes it. Everything else is detail."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Buckets, Not Groups",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Divides the result set into buckets",
            "Computation fully independent inside each bucket",
            "Omit PARTITION BY = one partition holding all rows",
            "Row count out always equals row count in"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Simple and Composite"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "AVG(salary) OVER (PARTITION BY department)",
            "-- each row + its own dept average",
            "ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY region, year",
            "  ORDER BY revenue DESC)  -- fresh per pair"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Anatomy of the OVER Clause",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Boundaries Reset Everything",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Ranking counters restart at 1 in each partition",
            "Running totals restart at the first row",
            "LAG on a partition's first row returns NULL",
            "It never reaches the previous partition's last row"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "NULL Keys"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "All rows with NULL key land in the same partition",
            "NULLs count as equal for partitioning",
            "Unlike = comparisons, where NULL = NULL is unknown"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Versus GROUP BY"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "GROUP BY",
            "PARTITION BY"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Output rows",
              "one per group",
              "one per input row"
            ],
            [
              "Detail cols",
              "must aggregate",
              "keep freely"
            ],
            [
              "Purpose",
              "summary",
              "detail + context"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Mix Windows Freely",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT SUM(x) OVER (PARTITION BY a),",
            "       SUM(x) OVER (PARTITION BY b)",
            "FROM t;  -- each column its own window"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Share-of-Group Pattern"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "amount / SUM(amount)",
            "  OVER (PARTITION BY category) * 100",
            "  AS pct_of_category"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Cardinality",
          "text": "However many partitions exist, output row count equals input row count. Windows never add or remove rows."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What It Establishes",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Row sequence for order-sensitive functions",
            "Rankings, offsets, cumulative aggregates need it",
            "Fully independent of the query-level ORDER BY",
            "Repeat it at query level to sort the output"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Silent Switch",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SUM(x) OVER (PARTITION BY g)",
            "  -- partition total on every row",
            "SUM(x) OVER (PARTITION BY g ORDER BY t)",
            "  -- running total up to current row"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Why it changes",
          "text": "Adding ORDER BY makes the default frame RANGE UNBOUNDED PRECEDING TO CURRENT ROW. No error, just a different number."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ranking Demands Order"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "ROW_NUMBER() OVER () is legal in some engines",
            "But numbering is then non-deterministic",
            "Always give ranking functions an ORDER BY"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "PARTITION BY: Slicing the Rows",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ties Are 'Peers'"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Construct",
            "Treats peers as"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "RANK / DENSE_RANK",
              "one unit"
            ],
            [
              "RANGE frame",
              "one unit"
            ],
            [
              "ROWS frame",
              "separate rows"
            ],
            [
              "ROW_NUMBER",
              "separate rows"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "NULL Placement",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "NULLS FIRST / NULLS LAST controls it explicitly",
            "PostgreSQL: NULLS LAST for ASC, FIRST for DESC",
            "MySQL: NULLs sort first for ASC",
            "Never rely on the default across engines"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Break Ties Yourself"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "ORDER BY score DESC, created_at ASC, id ASC",
            "-- id last = one unique total order"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Determinism rule",
          "items": [
            "No unique tiebreaker = unstable results",
            "Varies between runs and between engines",
            "Add the primary key as the final sort key"
          ],
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Big Three on 90, 90, 80",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Score",
            "ROW_NUMBER",
            "RANK",
            "DENSE_RANK"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "90",
              "1",
              "1",
              "1"
            ],
            [
              "90",
              "2",
              "1",
              "1"
            ],
            [
              "80",
              "3",
              "3",
              "2"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "ROW_NUMBER: 1,2,3... never ties, arbitrary among peers",
            "RANK: peers share, then a gap follows",
            "DENSE_RANK: peers share, no gap"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Picking One"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Need",
            "Use"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Dedup, pagination keys",
              "ROW_NUMBER"
            ],
            [
              "Competition standings",
              "RANK"
            ],
            [
              "Tier / level labels",
              "DENSE_RANK"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Buckets and Percentiles",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "NTILE(n): split ordered partition into n near-equal buckets",
            "Uneven split: earlier buckets get the extra rows",
            "PERCENT_RANK(): (rank-1)/(total-1), spans 0 to 1",
            "CUME_DIST(): fraction of rows at or before this value"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "ORDER BY Inside OVER",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Top-N Per Group"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT * FROM (",
            "  SELECT *, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (",
            "    PARTITION BY dept ORDER BY salary DESC",
            "  ) rn FROM emp) t WHERE rn <= 3;"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Deduplication"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "DELETE FROM t WHERE id IN (",
            " SELECT id FROM (SELECT id, ROW_NUMBER()",
            "  OVER (PARTITION BY email",
            "   ORDER BY created_at) rn FROM t) x",
            " WHERE rn > 1);  -- keep the oldest"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Hard Limits",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Ranking functions ignore the frame clause entirely",
            "ROWS with RANK: an error or a no-op, engine-dependent",
            "ROW_NUMBER cannot go in WHERE of the same SELECT",
            "Windows run after WHERE — wrap in a CTE to filter"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Base Accumulator",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SUM(amount) OVER (ORDER BY order_date",
            "  ROWS UNBOUNDED PRECEDING)",
            "-- first row .. current row"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Add PARTITION BY account_id to reset per account",
            "Accumulator restarts at each partition's first row"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Same Frame, Other Functions"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Function",
            "Gives"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "COUNT(*)",
              "1-based running sequence"
            ],
            [
              "AVG(x)",
              "average so far"
            ],
            [
              "MAX(x)",
              "best so far"
            ],
            [
              "MIN(x)",
              "worst so far"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Running COUNT(*) respects ties differently than ROW_NUMBER"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ledger Balance",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "opening + SUM(delta) OVER (",
            "  PARTITION BY account",
            "  ORDER BY posted_at, txn_id",
            "  ROWS UNBOUNDED PRECEDING) AS balance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Percent of Total So Far"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SUM(x) OVER (ORDER BY t",
            "  ROWS UNBOUNDED PRECEDING)",
            "  / SUM(x) OVER ()  -- two windows, one row"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Ranking Functions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Tie Trap",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Default frame with ORDER BY is RANGE, not ROWS",
            "RANGE lumps equal ORDER BY values into one step",
            "Two orders on one date both show the day-end total",
            "Fix: write ROWS UNBOUNDED PRECEDING explicitly",
            "Or add a unique tiebreaker to the window ORDER BY"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Counting Backwards"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SUM(x) OVER (ORDER BY t ROWS BETWEEN",
            "  CURRENT ROW AND UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING)",
            "-- remaining, not accumulated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "No nesting",
          "text": "SUM(SUM(x) OVER ()) OVER () is illegal. Layer window computations with a CTE or subquery instead."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Frame Grammar",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "{ROWS | RANGE | GROUPS}",
            "  BETWEEN <start> AND <end>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Bound",
            "Means"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "UNBOUNDED PRECEDING",
              "partition start"
            ],
            [
              "n PRECEDING",
              "n back"
            ],
            [
              "CURRENT ROW",
              "here"
            ],
            [
              "n FOLLOWING",
              "n ahead"
            ],
            [
              "UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING",
              "partition end"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Three Units",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Unit",
            "Counts",
            "Note"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "ROWS",
              "physical rows",
              "2 PRECEDING = 3 rows"
            ],
            [
              "RANGE",
              "ORDER BY value",
              "7 PRECEDING = 7 days"
            ],
            [
              "GROUPS",
              "peer groups",
              "tie-group steps"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "RANGE pulls in every peer row sharing the value",
            "GROUPS: PostgreSQL 11+, SQLite — not MySQL 8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Defaults You Inherit"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No ORDER BY: RANGE UNBOUNDED PRECEDING .. UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING",
            "That is the whole partition",
            "With ORDER BY: RANGE UNBOUNDED PRECEDING .. CURRENT ROW",
            "That is cumulative, through peers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Shorthand"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "ROWS UNBOUNDED PRECEDING",
            "== ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING",
            "     AND CURRENT ROW  -- start only implies end"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Running Totals",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "RANGE Offset Rules"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Numeric or interval offset needs exactly one ORDER BY column",
            "That column's type must be compatible with the offset",
            "RANGE n PRECEDING over a text column is illegal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Moving Averages",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "AVG(price) OVER (ORDER BY day",
            "  ROWS BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)",
            "-- trailing 7; centred: 3 PRECEDING AND 3 FOLLOWING"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Edges and EXCLUDE",
          "items": [
            "Frames truncate at partition start — early rows average fewer",
            "Guard: COUNT(*) OVER (same frame) >= 7",
            "EXCLUDE CURRENT ROW | GROUP | TIES | NO OTHERS",
            "EXCLUDE: PostgreSQL 11+ and SQLite, absent in MySQL"
          ],
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Signatures",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Call",
            "Returns"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "LAG(expr, off, def)",
              "row off back"
            ],
            [
              "LEAD(expr, off, def)",
              "row off ahead"
            ],
            [
              "off omitted",
              "defaults to 1"
            ],
            [
              "def omitted",
              "defaults to NULL"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Period-over-Period"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "amount - LAG(amount) OVER (",
            "  PARTITION BY sku ORDER BY month)",
            "-- month-on-month change"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Percent Change, Safely"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "(amount - LAG(amount) OVER w)",
            "  / NULLIF(LAG(amount) OVER w, 0)",
            "-- NULLIF guards divide-by-zero"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Gap Detection",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "WHERE event_time - LAG(event_time) OVER (",
            "  PARTITION BY session ORDER BY event_time)",
            "  > INTERVAL '30 minutes'  -- session break"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Frame-Sensitive Values"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "FIRST_VALUE / LAST_VALUE read the frame's first/last row",
            "They obey the frame; LAG and LEAD ignore it",
            "NTH_VALUE(expr, n) reads the nth row of the frame",
            "PostgreSQL adds FROM FIRST / FROM LAST; MySQL does not"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The LAST_VALUE Trap",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "LAST_VALUE(x) OVER (ORDER BY t)",
            "-- returns x of the CURRENT row!",
            "LAST_VALUE(x) OVER (ORDER BY t ROWS BETWEEN",
            " UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Why",
          "text": "The default frame ends at CURRENT ROW, so the frame's last row is you. Widen the frame and it works."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "LAG, LEAD and FIRST_VALUE",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "IGNORE NULLS",
          "items": [
            "Lets LAG / FIRST_VALUE skip NULLs",
            "Clean last-known-value forward fill",
            "Oracle, SQL Server 2022+, BigQuery, Snowflake",
            "PostgreSQL 16+; RESPECT NULLS is the default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Partition wall",
          "text": "LAG and LEAD always address rows relative to the whole partition, and never cross its boundary."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Head to Head",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "GROUP BY",
            "Window"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Rows out",
              "one per group",
              "one per input row"
            ],
            [
              "Other cols",
              "must be grouped",
              "any column allowed"
            ],
            [
              "Best for",
              "summary rows",
              "detail + context"
            ],
            [
              "Filtering",
              "HAVING",
              "outer query / QUALIFY"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "They Combine"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT dept, SUM(sal) t,",
            "  RANK() OVER (ORDER BY SUM(sal) DESC)",
            "FROM e GROUP BY dept;",
            "-- window runs on the grouped output"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Self-Join It Replaces",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "FROM t a JOIN t b ON b.date <= a.date",
            "GROUP BY a.id  -- O(n^2) comparisons",
            "-- window version: one sorted pass"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Correlated Subquery"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "(SELECT SUM(x) FROM t b WHERE b.d <= a.d)",
            "Re-executes once per outer row",
            "Usually far slower and harder to read"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "DISTINCT ON"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "PostgreSQL DISTINCT ON vs ROW_NUMBER() = 1",
            "DISTINCT ON is terser, often faster for one-row-per-group",
            "But it is non-portable — windows travel everywhere"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Readability",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Windows state 'per-row context' declaratively",
            "Self-joins bury the intent inside join predicates",
            "The reader must reconstruct the inequality's meaning"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When GROUP BY Still Wins"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
